# Replication package (v1): auditing consensus in Pol.is conversations

Code and results for the manuscript on certifying, with error control, the group-informed consensus
statements reported by Pol.is in 19 open conversations.

Contents
- `code/`: corpus construction (`corpus_polis.py`), certification and typing of consensus statements
  (`soic_polis.py`, `derived_i.py`), sensitivity to "pass" votes, ablation, split-sample replication,
  and the scripts that compute every figure quoted in the manuscript (`cifras_manuscrito.py`,
  `extras_manuscrito.py`, `figura1.py`). `build_manuscript.py` assembles the manuscript from the result files.
- `resultados/`: result files (JSON and CSV). File and variable names are in Spanish.

Data: the raw votes are the public Pol.is open data (https://github.com/compdemocracy/openData, CC BY 4.0)
and are not redistributed here except as the derived tables in `resultados/`.

Licence: code under MIT; result files under CC BY 4.0.

Archived at Zenodo: DOI 10.5281/zenodo.24218418
